{"ticker":"BUD","generated_at_utc":"2026-10-22T00:28:47.122233Z","profile":{"name":"Anheuser-Busch InBev SA/NV","exchange":"NYSE","country":"Belgium","sector":"Consumer Defensive","industry":"Beverages - Brewers","website":"https://www.ab-inbev.com","summary":"Anheuser-Busch InBev SA/NV produces and sells beer in North America, Middle Americas, South America, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. It operates through North America, Middle Americas, South America, EMEA, Asia Pacific, and Global Export and Holding Companies segments. The company also offers flavored malt beverages, soft drinks, spirit-based ready-to-drink cocktails and beverages, and energy drinks. In addition, it operates BEES, a business-to-business digital commerce platform; on-demand delivery platforms under the Z\u00e9 Delivery and TaDa Delivery brands; and premium at-home draft system under the PerfectDraft brand. The company provides a portfolio of approximately 500 beer brands, which primarily include Budweiser, Corona Extra, Michelob Ultra, and Stella Artois; Aguila, Brahma, Carling Black Label, Cass Fresh, Jupiler, Quilmes, SKOL, and Victoria; Beck's, Hoegaarden, and Leffe; Antarctica, Bud Light, Castle, Castle Lite, Cristal, Harbin, Modelo Especial, Sedrin, and Skol brands, as well as non-beer brands comprising Brutal Fruit, Cutwater, and N\u00dcTRL brands. The company was formerly known as InBev SA and changed its name to Anheuser-Busch InBev SA/NV in November 2008. Anheuser-Busch InBev SA/NV was founded in 1366 and is headquartered in Leuven, Belgium."},"stats":{"price":82.29,"marketCap":162039611392.0,"revenueGrowth":0.11,"operatingMargins":0.27341,"fcfMargin":0.17078375782084815,"netCash":-64721000448.0,"trailingPE":17.734915,"priceToSales":2.587872,"beta":0.779,"debtToEquity":0.7188,"fiftyTwoWeekLow":59.64,"fiftyTwoWeekHigh":86.6,"avgVolume":2119068.0},"bars":[{"d":"2025-10-22","o":61.68,"h":62.18,"l":61.25,"c":61.8,"v":2081000},{"d":"2025-10-23","o":61.64,"h":61.64,"l"